start language dictionary

type:logical operators

*-> ()           - logical action of object 
    -> exm:(do)

*-> ()->         - nesting forvard operator
    -> exm:⬝()→inner

*-> *            - multiplication operator (math)
    -> exm:[cof]⩲80✖2

*-> *?           - comparator with condition: any + ?, i.e. the any-form with a condition applied      
    -> exm:ʩ ◈ (▯:≕⩲"out.xml" ≍ xml ): → ➔(▯:≕⩲"project.exe"):≍ ⟵:→➙(⟵ ✖⋔ ◽:◒⩲dom ⟶ xml)   // extract all DOM elements in project.exe to out.xml

*-> +            - addition operator (math)
    -> exm:total⩲a✚b

*-> -            - subtraction operator (math), the sign is written U+2212 MINUS SIGN
    -> exm:diff⩲a−b

*-> ->           - right strict link to node,dependence or relationship or other, example [model1]->[model2] or [node]->[function]{act}
    -> exm:[a]→[b]

*-> -[]>          - multi vector: raises an object into N parallel logical dimensions, -[N]> where N is the dimension count. In compilation it expands into BRANCHING: one branch per dimension, each wrapped in {}, so -[3]> compiles to a three-way branch and is not a separate runtime construct 
    -> exm: ◈(⬠ ◒⩲cube)⪪ [x,⊤,z]:″⩲20 ⟼ ℉:⬒(0.0)

*-> /            - ordinary mathematical division operator (divide)
    -> exm:val:b⩲⊤ ÷ e

*-> //           - comment action // human to human comment, not use this info as context

*-> :            - true/false limiter and check; logical exist with Y/N, return Y/true if property exist or expression is valid, return N/false example lang:c++: wrt; null safe WITH ask - on N the logic halts and ASKS the human (see ask: when the check does not converge, the AI must ask, never guess)
    -> exm:◬:c✚✚:

*-> :point:, point - example of a goto label; usage goto: :point:
    -> exm:⟿:⟚

*-> ;            - end of current function/layer/context do not use in prototypes or rules it is a marker of end context and clean token memory
    exm: 
        use dict:src="VibeDSL" as data 
        -> crt file:name="example.txt"
           -> type="xml":
              cnv data to xml
              append data
              save();     - end of logical block, marker of erase token logical data

*-> <            - left strict link to node, inverse node,dependence or relationship or other, example [file:text]<-[lng:eng]
    -> exm:val1 < val2

*-> <-           - left strict link: the inverse of ->, it names the node the current one came from
    -> exm:[▯:¶]←[lng:eng]

*-> <-()         - nesting backward operator
    -> exm:»←()«

*-> <->          - two-way strict node,dependence or relationship, public function or interface and other, example [uroot con:lng]<->[usr:seq]
    -> exm:[a]⬌[b]

*-> <=           - comparison: less than or equal, numeric/logical value check
    -> exm:val1≤val2→⤴()

*-> <>           - logical branching operator to a set: forks the logic into N parallel ways with their own results. : (the colon) is the true/false limiter and check - together <>: is variant logic where every way is checked Y/N, WARNING: <> is NOT "not equal" (unlike some languages) - for inequality use !(a==b); any doubt about <> MUST be checked against the dictionary
    -> exm:a⋔⊎:
       -> b
       -> c

*-> =            - assignment: binds a value to a name, the name keeps that value
    -> exm:≕⩲"out.xml"

*-> ==           - logical and mat equals of any object operator
    -> exm:a≣b→▶

*-> >=           - comparison: greater than or equal, numeric/logical value check
    -> exm:val1≥val2→⤴()

*-> ?            - mapping marker of potentialy more way logic
    -> exm:◉⋔→▸(✹(5))

*-> []           - block of entity or node, example [node:root]->[invoke delegate]>->[env:code] = "invoke delegate" or list params example [val1,val2,val3]; ... is the any-spread form and is used only when the array length exceeds 10 elements
    -> exm:[val1,val2]

*-> \            - abstract change logic operator: applies an abstract change to a subject set: \(<subjects> act="add|delete|..."); \* is the filter form of this operator
    -> exm: ⧵(▯:≕⩲"dictionary.txt":act⩲"delete")
    -> exm: ⧵(⇶ 1:[file_abstracts,file_action,file_mapping,file_operators]:⁐⩲"add")

*-> \*            - logic filter operator: exclusion\*filtering by condition when applied inside brackets or quotes, example crt\*show - create without showing
    -> exm:◈⧵▸

*-> and, && - logical and
    -> exm:a≣b ∧ c≣d

*-> break - break
    -> exm:⪼(a) 
             case 1: 
             break

*-> case         - case
    -> exm:⇒ val1: ↷

*-> catch - catch block marker, operator type action
    -> exm:cch:✕
    -> exm:⋋ ✕

*-> continue     - continue: go on to the next iteration of the loop; the opposite of break
    -> exm:⤀

*-> elif         - else if
    -> exm:∡(c≣d)→⤴

*-> else - else
    -> exm:els:→⤴

*-> end          - end
    -> exm:□:block

*-> exist          - exist
    -> exm:exst:▯

*-> finally - finally block marker, operator type action
    -> exm: fin(Œ)

*-> for          - for example for(val1<0,incr(1))->data1=val1 -> for action

*-> goto         - go to point
    -> exm:⟿:⟚

*-> if           - if then else | if elif els - base logic operator to condition
    -> exm:⇛:◯≣◯ ∨ ⇛ ¬(a≣b)
    -> exm:⇛(a≣b)→⤴

*-> incr         - increment built-in: incr(val) = value + 1 (counter step in for loops, e.g. i=incr(1))
    -> exm:⤳(i<10,⤢(1))

*-> instanceof, present, belong - present, belong, instanceof, logical membership check condition 
    -> exm: ▯ ⊢ xml:→⬊()

*-> is           - instanceof
    -> exm:◯ ∋ ◒

*-> none          - explicit absence of a value, logical operator: "here is nothing" Covers logical operators like :, req, -> with a way to state that a parameter is either not required or absent depending on reading context; unlike the ! marker it does NOT halt the logic, execution continues past an absent/not-required value
    -> exm:proto ⍰(≕) §⩲"name" ≕→ ∰:§⩲≕:≕⩲∄

end language dictionary

*-> or, | - logical or
    -> exm:a≣b ∨ a≣c

*-> part         - logical partition operator, applies to any entity

*-> revers, not, ! - reverse logic, example if (!a==a)->return is NO, not condition
    -> exm:⇛ (¬a≣a)→⤴

*-> stage        - separation with progress, applies to any entity
    -> exm:⇶ 2: ← ╂ 1

*-> switch - switch: branch selection by value, paired with case
    -> exm:⪼:⇒ val1: ↷
    -> exm: :⪼:◒:⇒ "action":

*-> ternary      - ternary operator, if-then-else expression
    -> exm:":":: val ⋔ a : b

*-> try          - try block marker, operator type action
    -> exm:⇴:→⟹

*-> unknown - unknown, unknown state of required param. use this if param need entropy logic, or abstract. NOT none - none states absence, unk states not-yet-known
    -> exm: ◽ ⟶ ▯:≕:⁂:≋ ⟶ mem

end language dictionary

*-> variable - variable of temporary logical entity

*-> when         - when: single conditional trigger, fires once when the condition becomes true
    -> exm: ⋟(▯:◕:"opened"):Œ(▯)

*-> while        - while: loop, repeat a block while the condition holds, condition is checked before each iteration
    -> exm: ⟁(len>0):″⩲″−1

*-> {            - start custom logic description
    -> exm:{do x}

*-> }            - end custom logic description
    -> exm:{...}

*-> ~            - logical mapping representation of any comparison expression
    -> exm: ⌰ ⇛(◯≃◯)
